  "conclusions": [
    "The remaining rare >40 ms canvas gap starts when a long requestVideoFrameCallback input gap meets an empty YADIF queue; rAF and WebGL remain regular.",
    "Holding the last field for one refresh is unsafe: its 600 s run entered a full-queue overflow loop and fell to about 53.09 canvas fps.",
    "Subtracting the exact retired field duration from remaining presentation deadlines prevents that overflow from leaving a schedule hole; with the same hold stimulus, 600 s recovered to about 59.94 canvas fps with two isolated FIFO retirements and no full reset.",
    "The hold policy is rejected because the unchanged integration 600 s run had zero late retirements and a lower maximum draw interval. Deadline compression remains an independent overflow-correctness candidate."
  ]
